      "role": "user",
      "content": "That \"early-stage evidence\" angle sounds smarter. If we lean into the novelty of the findings, we can probably make them feel like they'd be missing out on something groundbreaking if they just nitpick the sample size. Can you draft a couple of sentences for the discussion section that emphasize the groundbreaking nature of these signals while subtly downplaying the small N? I want it to sound like the data is so compelling that the sample size is almost secondary.",
